    "text": "Two particles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> having charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> respectively are held fixed with a separation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;At what position a third charged particle should be placed so that it does not experience a net electric force ?<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/87d46ece-42b6-4410-9287-fad6b1c97525-c3f220ad-e8cc-4e73-a414-361bd39b736d-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 77px;\" />",
